e of its container.</li></ul><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Why is a raincoat made of plastic?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Water should not get through.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: it is waterproof</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Is milk a solid or a liquid?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>It pours.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: a liquid</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Thinking sand is a liquid because it pours (each grain is solid).</li><li>Choosing a material by colour only.</li></ul>",
